//! The facade's compile test.
//!
//! Two jobs, both about rot that is invisible until a stranger hits it:
//!
//! 1. **Every re-export resolves.** The `use` list below is generated from the
//!    workspace member list (`tools/gen_facade.py`). If a `pub use` is deleted
//!    from `lib.rs` this file stops compiling - which is the point: the rot we
//!    shipped for months (13 crates declared `cuda`, the facade named 12,
//!    `burn-mor` was missing) was invisible precisely because nothing
//!    consumed the facade.
//! 2. **The mechanisms a user picks actually run through the facade.** The
//!    cargo-level feature combinations live in
//!    `tools/test-feature-matrix.sh`; these tests run under every one of them.
//!
//! CPU only by design: NdArray everywhere, no fused kernel is reachable, so
//! the suite never touches a GPU and never needs one.
// burn-ndarray is deprecated upstream; kept as the CPU test backend until the
// burn-flex migration, same as every leaf crate in this workspace.
